I'm about ready to book the conference room for LogFest.

I have some question for everybody:

1.  Are you expecting to come to LogFest?  It will be in FairFax, VA
(which is right next to DC) on the 25th-27th of July (i.e. the
weekend of the 25th).

2.  If you are coming to LogFest, are you able to pay for your own
hotel room?  They'll likely run around $90 a night.

    A)  If so, do you mind someone sharing your room?

    B)  If not, do you mind sharing someone else's room and
    contributing to that room's costs?

3.  How much would you be willing to pay to support LogFest?

To give people a sense of scale, the conference room is likely to be
$100-$150/day.  If we book it for only Saturday and Sunday, that's
still $200-$300.

Please answer quickly, because I need to book the hotel!

